g","depth":3,"id":"debugging-key-display","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debugging key display"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    formatForDisplay,\n    getHeldKeyCodesMap,\n    getHeldKeys,\n    type RegisterableHotkey,\n  } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const heldKeys = getHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = getHeldKeyCodesMap()\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each heldKeys.keys as key}\n    <kbd>\n      {formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })}:\n      {heldCodes.codes[key] ?? 'unknown'}\n    </kbd>\n  {/each}\n</div>","lang":"svelte"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"under-the-hood","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Under the hood"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All three functions subscribe to the singleton "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"KeyStateTracker"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\ntracker.getHeldKeys()\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"modifier-held-shortcut-hints","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Modifier-held shortcut hints"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getHotkeyHint"},{"type":"text","value":" answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const hint = getHotkeyHint(() => binding) // reactive getter: hint.visible","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Alt+Shift+[KeyK]"},{"type":"text","value":", holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ exact: true }"},{"type":"text","value":" to require all binding modifiers, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ platform: 'mac' }"},{"type":"text","value":" to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Combine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"getheldkeys","text":"getHeldKeys","level":2},{"id":"getheldkeycodesmap","text":"getHeldKeyCodesMap","level":2},{"id":"getiskeyheld","text":"getIsKeyHeld","level":2},{"id":"common-patterns","text":"Common patterns","level":2},{"id":"hold-to-reveal-ui","text":"Hold-to-reveal UI","level":3},{"id":"debugging-key-display","text":"Debugging key display","level":3},{"id":"under-the-hood","text":"Under the hood","level":2},{"id":"modifier-held-shortcut-hints","text":"Modifier-held shortcut hints","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nTanStack Hotkeys provides three Svelte functions for tracking live keyboard state: `getHeldKeys`, `getHeldKeyCodesMap`, and `getIsKeyHeld`.\n\n## `getHeldKeys`\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { getHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const heldKeys = getHeldKeys()\n</script>\n\n<div>{heldKeys.keys.length > 0 ? heldKeys.keys.join(' + ') : 'No keys held'}</div>\n```\n\n## `getHeldKeyCodesMap`\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { getHeldKeyCodesMap } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const heldCodes = getHeldKeyCodesMap()\n</script>\n\n<pre>{JSON.stringify(heldCodes.codes, null, 2)}</pre>\n```\n\n## `getIsKeyHeld`\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { getIsKeyHeld } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const isShiftHeld = getIsKeyHeld('Shift')\n</script>\n\n<span class:active={isShiftHeld.held}>Shift</span>\n```\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Hold-to-reveal UI\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { getIsKeyHeld } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const isShiftHeld = getIsKeyHeld('Shift')\n</script>\n\n{#if isShiftHeld.held}\n  <button>Permanently Delete</button>\n{:else}\n  <button>Move to Trash</button>\n{/if}\n```\n\n### Debugging key display\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    formatForDisplay,\n    getHeldKeyCodesMap,\n    getHeldKeys,\n    type RegisterableHotkey,\n  } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const heldKeys = getHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = getHeldKeyCodesMap()\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each heldKeys.keys as key}\n    <kbd>\n      {formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })}:\n      {heldCodes.codes[key] ?? 'unknown'}\n    </kbd>\n  {/each}\n</div>\n```\n\n## Under the hood\n\nAll three functions subscribe to the singleton `KeyStateTracker`:\n\n```ts\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\ntracker.getHeldKeys()\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')\n```\n\n## Modifier-held shortcut hints\n\n`getHotkeyHint` answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:\n\n```ts\nconst hint = getHotkeyHint(() => binding) // reactive getter: hint.visible\n```\n\nFor `Alt+Shift+[KeyK]`, holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass `{ exact: true }` to require all binding modifiers, or `{ platform: 'mac' }` to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection.\n\nCombine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is `matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Key State Tracking Guide\nid: key-state-tracking\n---\n\nTanStack Hotkeys provides three Svelte functions for tracking live keyboard state: `getHeldKeys`, `getHeldKeyCodesMap`, and `getIsKeyHeld`.\n\n## `getHeldKeys`\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { getHeldKeys } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const heldKeys = getHeldKeys()\n</script>\n\n<div>{heldKeys.keys.length > 0 ? heldKeys.keys.join(' + ') : 'No keys held'}</div>\n```\n\n## `getHeldKeyCodesMap`\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { getHeldKeyCodesMap } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const heldCodes = getHeldKeyCodesMap()\n</script>\n\n<pre>{JSON.stringify(heldCodes.codes, null, 2)}</pre>\n```\n\n## `getIsKeyHeld`\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { getIsKeyHeld } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const isShiftHeld = getIsKeyHeld('Shift')\n</script>\n\n<span class:active={isShiftHeld.held}>Shift</span>\n```\n\n## Common patterns\n\n### Hold-to-reveal UI\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import { getIsKeyHeld } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const isShiftHeld = getIsKeyHeld('Shift')\n</script>\n\n{#if isShiftHeld.held}\n  <button>Permanently Delete</button>\n{:else}\n  <button>Move to Trash</button>\n{/if}\n```\n\n### Debugging key display\n\n```svelte\n<script lang=\"ts\">\n  import {\n    formatForDisplay,\n    getHeldKeyCodesMap,\n    getHeldKeys,\n    type RegisterableHotkey,\n  } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\n  const heldKeys = getHeldKeys()\n  const heldCodes = getHeldKeyCodesMap()\n</script>\n\n<div>\n  {#each heldKeys.keys as key}\n    <kbd>\n      {formatForDisplay(key as RegisterableHotkey, { useSymbols: true })}:\n      {heldCodes.codes[key] ?? 'unknown'}\n    </kbd>\n  {/each}\n</div>\n```\n\n## Under the hood\n\nAll three functions subscribe to the singleton `KeyStateTracker`:\n\n```ts\nimport { getKeyStateTracker } from '@tanstack/svelte-hotkeys'\n\nconst tracker = getKeyStateTracker()\ntracker.getHeldKeys()\ntracker.isKeyHeld('Shift')\n```\n\n## Modifier-held shortcut hints\n\n`getHotkeyHint` answers whether held modifiers are relevant to a binding. Keep formatting and badge styling in your component:\n\n```ts\nconst hint = getHotkeyHint(() => binding) // reactive getter: hint.visible\n```\n\nFor `Alt+Shift+[KeyK]`, holding Alt, Shift, or both reveals the hint. An extra Control hides it; releasing all modifiers or blurring the window hides it. Nonmodifier keys are ignored. AltGraph does not reveal hints. Pass `{ exact: true }` to require all binding modifiers, or `{ platform: 'mac' }` to resolve Mod explicitly. Supply the same platform used by the registration when overriding detection.\n\nCombine the boolean with the action's enabled state. The helper does not register a shortcut or determine whether its target is focused. The core equivalent is `matchesHeldModifiers(binding, heldKeys, options)`.\n"}
